ask(c,'For c2=−1/2 and s2=√3/2, which θ2 is returned by atan2(s2,c2) in(−180°,180°]?', ['120°','−60°','30°','−120°'], ['Positive sine and negative cosine put the angle in quadrantII.','Using arctan(s/c) alone loses the quadrant and gives−60°.','That would have positive cosine and a different ratio.','Negative120° has negative sine.'],kind='numerical',steps=['Identify sine>0 and cosine<0, hence quadrantII.','The reference angle is60°.','θ2=180°−60°=120°.'],assumptions=['Degrees; standard atan2(y,x) argument order and stated principal interval.'])
